WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.545
Zheng Chenggong (Koxinga) was a brave general in the late Ming dynasty.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.550
He hoped to hold onto a peaceful and stable land.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.370
The common people by the sea all came to see the fleet off.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.530
In the year 1661, he led the fleet and set sail.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.957
The large ships crossed the strait and arrived at the coast of Taiwan.

00:00:17.957 --> 00:00:21.275
Although the wind and waves were very strong, the sailors were completely unafraid.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:24.450
By the sea stood a castle built by the Dutch.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.790
The city walls were very high, and the defenders refused to surrender easily.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:31.241
Zheng Chenggong surrounded the castle and patiently waited for the right opportunity.

00:00:31.241 --> 00:00:35.404
Many months passed, and the food inside the city grew less and less.

00:00:35.404 --> 00:00:38.400
The people inside the castle also began to grow restless and unsettled.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:42.522
In the year 1662, the Dutch defenders finally surrendered.

00:00:42.522 --> 00:00:45.150
They handed over the castle and left Taiwan by ship.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:50.640
On this day, Taiwan's history turned a new page.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.133
Zheng Chenggong established a stable life in Taiwan.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:56.657
People resumed farming and fishing, living and working in peace and contentment.
